{title: Best Part of the Land}
{subtitle: Genesis 46:21; 46:26–27; 47:11–12; Numbers 26:38–39}
{key: E}
{tempo: 90}
{time: 4/4}

{comment: Verse (instrumental)}
| [E] | [E] | [E] | [E] |
| [E] | [B] |

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[C#m]Ten sons of Benjamin stand in [A]the list
[E]Bela and Becher [B]and Ashbel too
[C#m]Gera and Naaman fol[A]low the [E]line
Ehi is named [B]among the few
[C#m]Rosh and Muppim and Huppim [A]and [E]Ard
Names written in [B]the sacred scroll
[A]Jacob's family gathering [B]tight
[E]Ready to fol[B]low Joseph's [C#m]call [B]
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
[E]Settled in the [B]best part of [A]the [E]land
Food provid[B]ed for every [C#m]child [B]
[A]Pharaoh command[B]ed the d[E]welling place
Peace found in the Gos[B]hen field
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[C#m]Six-ty-six souls came with [A]Jacob
[E]Plus two born to Joseph [B]in Egypt
[C#m]Seventy persons in to[A]tal count
[E]Going down where the fa[B]mine was
Joseph [C#m]gave property to his [A]kin
[E]In the district of Ra[B]meses they stayed
[A]Clans of Benjamin recor[B]ded [E]well
Ahiramite [B]clan stands a[C#m]part [B]
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}

{start_of_bridge: Bridge}
From [C#m]Bela to Ashbel to Ahi[A]ram
[E]The census counts the [B]men again
Shup[A]ham and Hupham keep [B]their names
A lega[E]cy for future [B]days
{end_of_bridge}

{start_of_verse: Outro}
Ehi son [A]of Benjamin
Remembered in the ge[E]nealogy
{end_of_verse}
